        {
          "id": 1567677124,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> yes i known but i don't see where is the desc\n\nepan/dissectors/asn1/ros/ros-rej.cnf contains one of them.\n\n> but also gcc is not happy with change....\n\nDifferent compilers' data flow analyses may be different, with compiler 1's data flow analysis not being sufficient to determine that variable X will never be used when not initialized, and compiler 2's data flow analysis being sufficient to detect that *and* to, if you've worked around compiler 1's deficiencies by initializing the variable when declaring it, complain (at least when being used in full Clang Static Humiliator mode) that the initialization isn't needed because it's overwritten in all code paths where the variable is used.\n\nWhen you're dealing with the Dueling Compiler Problem, you may have to live with compiler 2's warnings (especially if they're just static analyzer warnings that don't break the build) in order to avoid compiler 1's warnings.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
